      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): defer session snapshot update after newSession/resumeSession result",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`newSession()` and `resumeSession()` in the ACP bridge send the `session_info_update` notification via `sendSessionSnapshotUpdate` BEFORE returning the JSON-RPC result. Clients that key off `session_info_update` to learn the sessionId receive a notification referencing a sessionId they have not yet parsed from the result.\n\nThis causes Rabbit R1 sessions to hang indefinitely (rabbit-agent gates prompt delivery on receiving session_info_update after the result).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe fix defers the notification and subsequent `sendAvailableCommands` to fire asynchronously after the result is returned, using the existing `void + .then() + .catch()` pattern already established in this file (line 316).\n\nBoth `newSession()` (line 394) and `resumeSession()` (line 554) are fixed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nClients that expect session_info_update after the session/new result now receive correct ordering. No change to the API contract, response shape, or notification content.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests\n```\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  19 passed (19)\n```\n\n### Typecheck\n```\npnpm tsgo:core — EXIT: 0\n```\n\n### Fix logic (newSession)\nBefore: `await sendSessionSnapshotUpdate(...)` → `return { sessionId, ... }`\nAfter:  `return { sessionId, ... }` → `void sendSessionSnapshotUpdate(...).then(...)`\n\nNotification fires asynchronously after the JSON-RPC result, so clients always receive sessionId before session_info_update.",
        "branch": "fix/acp-bridge-session-order",
